<title>POLAND: POLISH C.BANK OFFERS REVREPO, NBP-BILL SALE.</title>
<headline>POLISH C.BANK OFFERS REVREPO, NBP-BILL SALE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland</p>
<p>offered to drain 400 million zlotys, in nominal terms, off the</p>
<p>market for 14 days through a reverse NBP-bill repurchase</p>
<p>auction, the bank said.</p>
<p>Full details below.</p>
<p>    Deadline hour		 - 12:00</p>
<p>    Date of settlement	  - 3 OCT 96</p>
<p>    Repurchase		    - 17 OCT 96</p>
<p>    Discount rate (pct)	 - 20.00</p>
<p>Maturity of bills offered - 31 OCT 96</p>
<p>The bank also offered to sell 300 million zlotys worth of</p>
<p>its 273-day bills to domestic banks.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
